---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Patio Privacy Planner" description="Create a patio privacy worksheet with a spatial boundary preview, example screen counts, optional cost arithmetic, and a practical checklist."><header class="container page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Free planning tool · No account needed</p><h1>Patio Privacy Planner</h1><p class="lead">Map your patio or balcony, add its roof, walls, railing, and furniture, then compare a privacy-screen layout in 3D.</p></header><section class="container section planner-layout"><form class="panel planner-form" id="privacy-form" novalidate><fieldset><legend><span>1</span> Measure your space</legend><label for="space">Outdoor space</label><select id="space"><option value="patio">Ground-level patio</option><option value="balcony">Balcony</option></select><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="patio-width">Outdoor width (ft)</label><input id="patio-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="1" data-max="100" value="10" required/></div><div><label for="depth">Outdoor depth (ft)</label><input id="depth" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="2" data-max="100" value="8" required/></div></div><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="width">Width to screen (ft)</label><input id="width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="1" data-max="100" value="6" required/></div><div><label for="screen-height">Top of screen above floor (ft)</label><input id="screen-height" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="1" data-max="10" value="6" required/></div></div><p class="small">Plan one straight boundary. Screen height is measured from the floor, including when screening starts above a railing. It is a preference to research, not a safe-height recommendation.</p><label for="screen-side">Side to screen</label><select id="screen-side"><option value="back">A · far side (outdoor width)</option><option value="right">B · right side (outdoor depth)</option><option value="front">C · near side (outdoor width)</option><option value="left">D · left side (outdoor depth)</option></select><p class="small">A is the far edge in the drawing, C is nearest to you. B is right, D is left. These are drawing labels, not compass directions.</p></fieldset>
<fieldset><legend><span>2</span> Add the existing structure</legend>
<label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" id="has-roof"/> There is a roof over this space</label><div id="roof-fields" hidden><label for="roof-height">Roof underside above floor (ft)</label><input id="roof-height" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="2" data-max="30" value="8" disabled required/><p class="small">Shown as a flat roof covering the full area. Adding a roof does not automatically mean a sheltered site.</p></div>
<p class="field-title">Existing solid walls</p><div class="side-options"><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="wall-side" value="back"/> A · far</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="wall-side" value="right"/> B · right</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="wall-side" value="front"/> C · near</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="wall-side" value="left"/> D · left</label></div><div id="wall-fields" hidden><label for="wall-height">Existing wall height (ft)</label><input id="wall-height" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="1" data-max="30" value="8" disabled required/></div>
<label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" id="has-railing"/> There is an existing railing</label><div id="rail-fields" hidden><label for="rail-height">Railing height above floor (ft)</label><input id="rail-height" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.5" data-max="10" value="3.5" disabled required/><p class="field-title">Sides with a railing</p><div class="side-options"><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="rail-side" value="back" checked/> A · far</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="rail-side" value="right" /> B · right</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="rail-side" value="front" /> C · near</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="rail-side" value="left" /> D · left</label></div><label for="screen-mode">Where should the screen start?</label><select id="screen-mode"><option value="full">From the floor — including across the railing</option><option value="above">Only above the railing</option></select><p class="small">This specifies visual coverage, not attachment to the railing. Existing guards and permitted fixing methods need separate checks.</p></div></fieldset>
<fieldset><legend><span>3</span> Place basic furniture</legend><label for="furniture">Example furniture</label><select id="furniture"><option value="none">No furniture</option><option value="bistro">Two chairs and a small table</option><option value="bench">Bench and coffee table</option></select><div id="furniture-fields" hidden><label for="furniture-position">Position near side C</label><select id="furniture-position"><option value="center">Center</option><option value="left">Left</option><option value="right">Right</option></select><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="seat-width">Each seat / bench width (ft)</label><input id="seat-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.5" data-max="20" value="2" disabled required/></div><div><label for="seat-depth">Seat / bench depth (ft)</label><input id="seat-depth" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.5" data-max="20" value="2" disabled required/></div></div><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="table-width">Table width (ft)</label><input id="table-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.5" data-max="20" value="2" disabled required/></div><div><label for="table-depth">Table depth (ft)</label><input id="table-depth" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.5" data-max="20" value="2" disabled required/></div></div><p class="small">Enter actual footprints. Furniture is placed near C with example 0.5-ft spacing between pieces, not recommended walking clearance. Check doors and access separately.</p></div></fieldset>
<fieldset><legend><span>4</span> Choose an approach & check the site</legend><p class="small">Your priority changes the advice. Wind exposure and balcony permission determine which checks come first. Roof and wall choices do not automatically establish wind shelter.</p><label for="need">What matters most?</label><select id="need"><option value="view">Block a direct sightline</option><option value="flex">Easy to move or store</option><option value="green">Add greenery</option></select><label for="exposure">Wind exposure</label><select id="exposure"><option value="exposed" selected>Exposed or unsure</option><option value="sheltered">Sheltered; product limits still apply</option></select><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" id="approved"/> For a balcony, I have confirmed permission, permitted loads, drainage, and wind restrictions with building management.</label></fieldset><fieldset><legend><span>5</span> Compare an example layout</legend><label for="panel-width">Usable width per example module (ft)</label><input id="panel-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="1" data-max="10" value="3" required/><p class="small">Use an actual product's usable width if known. The default is a paper-layout assumption, not a product recommendation. Supports and overlaps may change fit. Use a decimal point or comma (for example, 2.16 or 2,16).</p><details class="cost-details"><summary>Optional: estimate using your own prices</summary><label for="module-price">Price per module (USD)</label><input id="module-price" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0" data-max="100000" placeholder="Leave blank if unknown"/><label for="extra-cost">Additional costs (USD)</label><input id="extra-cost" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0" data-max="100000" value="0"/><p class="small">Include supports, delivery, or taxes in additional costs. No prices are retrieved from retailers.</p></details></fieldset><div class="plan-actions"><button class="button" type="submit">Create my plan →</button><button class="reset-button" type="reset">Start over</button></div><p class="small">Your answers stay in this page. Nothing is sent to us or stored automatically.</p><noscript><p>JavaScript is needed for the interactive worksheet. Read our <a href="/articles/patio-privacy-ideas-for-renters/">patio privacy guide</a> for the planning steps.</p></noscript></form><section class="panel planner-result" aria-label="Your patio privacy worksheet"><h2>Your privacy plan</h2><div id="results" role="region" aria-label="Planner results" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" tabindex="-1"><div class="planner-empty"><p class="eyebrow">Example only · 10 × 8 ft patio</p><div id="planner-preview" aria-label="Example spatial layout"></div><h3>See where your screening would go.</h3><p>The floor shows your outdoor width and depth. The upright modules show an example screen along one boundary — including the height you enter.</p><div class="preview-key"><span><i class="key-floor"></i>Outdoor floor</span><span><i class="key-screen"></i>Example screening</span></div><p class="small">This example has two 3-foot modules, covering a 6-foot target. Create your plan to replace it with your measurements. Add your roof, walls, railing, and furniture to make this example your own. Safe installation and walking clearance are not assessed.</p></div></div></section></section><section class="container planner-guidance"><h2>What this tool does</h2><p>It visualizes a rectangular space with a full-area flat roof, solid walls, selected railing sides, basic furniture footprints, and one straight screening boundary. It compares starting approaches and calculates example coverage. It does not select or test products, determine required supports, assess wind or loads, check building codes, or guarantee privacy at a particular height.</p><p>Read the <a href="/articles/patio-privacy-ideas-for-renters/">patio privacy guide</a> or <a href="/articles/small-patio-furniture-layout/">small patio layout guide</a> before making changes.</p></section><script type="module" src="/assets/planner.js?v=room-20261014" is:inline></script></Base>
